**C-<<Cn1>>. DID NEXUSAI PULL REQUESTS 230 AND 231 LAND ON MAIN, WHAT DO THEY DO TO RD-793 AND RD-990, WHAT DID THE INDEPENDENT REVIEW FIND, AND WHAT STAYS OPEN? (landings recorded by the coordinator; it decides nothing new)** This entry is a record: it carries no ruling of its own and changes none; it touches the CodeQL policy (C-190), the open window rule (C-178) and the demo deploy hold (C-224) by reference only; any demo deploy is separate from this record. Provenance: pulls/230 and pulls/231 with their file lists and commits, the merge commits named below, the check-runs and workflow runs of each, the hosted code scan check run of the head of 231, main's code scanning analyses and alerts read <<READ-DATE>> (<<CHECKS-LIST>>; <<BUILD-LIST>>; <<ALERTS>>), the independent review of the branch of 231 (the gate's verdict, read whole, kept outside this repository), the builder's record, the tickets and their comments, and the Jira reads and writes of <<READ-DATE>>. Nothing was built, run, sent or put on a host by this step.
**What landed.** <<LANDED231>> <<LANDED230>>
**The independent review.** One round read the branch of 231 against main at the merge of 230: GO WITH FINDINGS, no Blocker, no Major (NO GO 0 of 1 round). F1 Minor, new with RD-990: the helper requestPath records the request target as sent, so an absolute-form target keeps its scheme and host in the audit path field and a raw # keeps the text after it (main recorded neither; the true route stays in the row; browsers send neither form); ticketed, not fixed before landing. F2 Minor, follow-up severity Medium: the two connection-test routes and the two reads discover-tables and describe-table still answer a signed-in viewer and make the server connect with the stored sign-in details of a source (one connect attempt for each test route and for discover-tables, three for describe-table; the response bodies of the test routes carry connection diagnostics; no data changes). F3 Minor: the header comment of the older test file for RD-988 still says the server file holds 30 calls of the administrator check (line 25) while its title and assertion say 34; a note, no ticket. F4 Minor, process: the builder's corrections (three lock acquisitions, a stray cd in a subshell, a reset entry written by worktree creation, files read by section) were judged true, with no effect on the product. F5 Observation: three test-shape notes (a quoted request key, a bounded wait loop, the committed inventory's origin field). Rows that PASS: exactly ten paths with the commissioned counts; the six hunks of the server file; the RD-994 block unchanged at five commits (same prefix, control: one flipped byte changes it); the merge clean and its tree equal to the head tree; 216 attempts by a viewer, a non-administrator and an anonymous caller changed no source at the head against 8 changes on main, with the administrator control changing a source 8 of 8; the sign-in configured but not enforced and the open window as described; the inventory (rows 203 and 203, route set equal, exactly four rows differ bet